concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-telecommunications-interception-and-other-measures-act-2005-sch-1-sec-1 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "1 Section 473.1 of the Criminal Code (at the end of the"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-1 ;
    values:originalText "definition of law enforcement officer) Add:  (g) a member of the New South Wales Crime Commission or a member of the staff of that Commission;  (h) an officer of the Independent Commission Against Corruption of New South Wales, being a person who is an officer as defined by the Independent Commission Against Corruption Act 1988 of New South Wales;  (i) the Commissioner of the Police Integrity Commission of New South Wales, an Assistant Commissioner of that Commission or a member of the staff of that Commission;  (j) an officer of the Corruption and Crime Commission of Western Australia within the meaning of the Corruption and Crime Commission Act 2003 of Western Australia;  (k) an authorised commission officer of the Crime and Misconduct Commission of Queensland within the meaning of the Crime and Misconduct Act 2001 of Queensland.  Amendment of the Telecommunications (Interception) Act 1979  Schedule 2 Emergency services  Part 1  Crimes Legislation Amendment (Telecommunications Interception and Other Measures) Act 2005 No. 95, 2005            5" ;
    skos:definition "definition of law enforcement officer) Add:  (g) a member of the New South Wales Crime Commission or a member of the staff of that Commission;  (h) an officer of the Independent Commission Against Corruption of New South Wales, being a person who is an officer as defined by the Independent Commission Against Corruption Act 1988 of New South Wales;  (i) the Commissioner of the Police Integrity Commission of New South Wales, an Assistant Commissioner of that Commission or a member of the staff of that Commission;  (j) an officer of the Corruption and Crime Commission of Western Australia within the meaning of the Corruption and Crime Commission Act 2003 of Western Australia;  (k) an authorised commission officer of the Crime and Misconduct Commission of Queensland within the meaning of the Crime and Misconduct Act 2001 of Queensland.  Amendment of the Telecommunications (Interception) Act 1979  Schedule 2 Emergency services  Part 1  Crimes Legislation Amendment (Telecommunications Interception and Other Measures) Act 2005 No. 95, 2005            5"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "aa958a34d98abcc629f2acddc63b003e0858fd8357a747b36ff9722bb8ec979b" ;
    cof:pageNumber "8"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "List of law enforcement officers and officials" ;
